exports[`Spanish: snapshot, translated letter text and placeholders 1`] = `
"<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="es">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Solicitud de devolución del depósito de garantía</title>
<style>
@page { margin: 20mm; }
body { font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif; color: #111; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0; }
.disclaimer { border: 2px solid #b3261e; color: #b3261e; padding: 6pt 8pt; margin: 0 0 18pt; font-family: -apple-system, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; }
.placeholder { background: #fff3c4; }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 6pt 0 12pt; font-size: 10pt; }
th, td { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 4pt 6pt; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
th { background: #f2f2f2; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<p class="disclaimer"><strong>No es asesoramiento legal.</strong> Esta es una plantilla completada con los datos de su inspección. Revise las leyes de su estado o localidad y edite todo lo que esté entre corchetes antes de enviarla.</p>
<p>2027-01-03</p>
<p>Pat Owner<br><span class="placeholder">[Dirección postal del arrendador]</span></p>
<p><strong>Asunto: Devolución del depósito de garantía de 12 Elm St, Unidad 4B</strong></p>
<p>Estimado/a Pat Owner:</p>
<p>Alquilé 12 Elm St, Unidad 4B, me mudé el 2026-01-02 y desocupé la vivienda el 2027-01-01. Le escribo para solicitar que me devuelva la totalidad de mi depósito de garantía de <span class="placeholder">[Monto del depósito]</span>, o que me envíe una lista detallada de cualquier deducción.</p>
<p>In California, landlords generally have 21 days after move-out to return the deposit. Itemized statement and any refund are both due within 21 days. Según esa norma, el depósito vence alrededor del 2027-01-22. Fuente (resumen en inglés): https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=CIV&amp;sectionNum=1950.5.</p>
<p>Documenté el estado de la vivienda a la entrada y a la salida. 2 elementos quedaron registrados en el mismo estado o en mejor estado a la salida.</p>
<p>La comparación indica que 2 elementos estaban en peor estado a la salida que a la entrada. Los incluyo aquí para que podamos hablarlo abiertamente, y le pido que cualquier deducción por ellos se detalle con recibos o presupuestos y refleje solo daños que excedan el desgaste normal:</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Habitación</th><th>Elemento</th><th>Entrada</th><th>Salida</th><th>Nota</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Kitchen</td><td>Oven</td><td>Bueno</td><td>Dañado</td><td>Scorch mark on door</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bath</td><td>Mirror</td><td>Bueno</td><td>Regular</td><td></td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>El informe de comparación de entrada y salida adjunto contiene fotos fechadas de la vivienda con fecha y hora del servidor. Se puede verificar con el código abcdef012345 en unscratched.app/v/abcdef012345.</p>
<p>Le pido que envíe el depósito a <span class="placeholder">[Dirección para recibir el depósito]</span>. Gracias por su ayuda.</p>
<p>Atentamente,<br>Sam Renter</p>
</body>
</html>
"
`;

exports[`snapshot of the full letter 1`] = `
"<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Security deposit return request</title>
<style>
@page { margin: 20mm; }
body { font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif; color: #111; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0; }
.disclaimer { border: 2px solid #b3261e; color: #b3261e; padding: 6pt 8pt; margin: 0 0 18pt; font-family: -apple-system, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; }
.placeholder { background: #fff3c4; }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 6pt 0 12pt; font-size: 10pt; }
th, td { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 4pt 6pt; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
th { background: #f2f2f2; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<p class="disclaimer"><strong>Not legal advice.</strong> This is a template prefilled from your inspection. Check your state or local law and edit anything in brackets before sending.</p>
<p>2027-01-03</p>
<p>Pat Owner<br><span class="placeholder">[Landlord mailing address]</span></p>
<p><strong>Re: Return of security deposit for 12 Elm St, Unit 4B</strong></p>
<p>Dear Pat Owner,</p>
<p>I rented 12 Elm St, Unit 4B and moved in on 2026-01-02. I moved out on 2027-01-01. I am writing to ask that my security deposit of <span class="placeholder">[Deposit amount]</span> be returned in full, or that you send an itemized list of any deductions.</p>
<p>In California, landlords generally have 21 days after move-out to return the deposit. Itemized statement and any refund are both due within 21 days. By that rule the deposit is due around 2027-01-22. Source: https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=CIV&amp;sectionNum=1950.5.</p>
<p>I documented the unit's condition at move-in and at move-out. 2 items were recorded in the same or better condition at move-out.</p>
<p>The comparison marks 2 items as being in worse condition at move-out than at move-in. I list them here so we can discuss them openly, and I ask that any deduction for them be itemized with receipts or estimates and reflect only damage beyond normal wear and tear:</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Room</th><th>Item</th><th>Move-in</th><th>Move-out</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Kitchen</td><td>Oven</td><td>Good</td><td>Damaged</td><td>Scorch mark on door</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bath</td><td>Mirror</td><td>Good</td><td>Fair</td><td></td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>The attached move-in vs move-out comparison report has dated photos of the unit with server timestamps. It can be checked with verification code abcdef012345 at unscratched.app/v/abcdef012345.</p>
<p>Please send the deposit to <span class="placeholder">[Forwarding address]</span>. Thank you for your help.</p>
<p>Sincerely,<br>Sam Renter</p>
</body>
</html>
"
`;

exports[`with a deposit split: snapshot with the deposit, itemized deductions, and each roommate's refund 1`] = `
"<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Security deposit return request</title>
<style>
@page { margin: 20mm; }
body { font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif; color: #111; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0; }
.disclaimer { border: 2px solid #b3261e; color: #b3261e; padding: 6pt 8pt; margin: 0 0 18pt; font-family: -apple-system, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; }
.placeholder { background: #fff3c4; }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 6pt 0 12pt; font-size: 10pt; }
th, td { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 4pt 6pt; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
th { background: #f2f2f2; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<p class="disclaimer"><strong>Not legal advice.</strong> This is a template prefilled from your inspection. Check your state or local law and edit anything in brackets before sending.</p>
<p>2027-01-03</p>
<p>Pat Owner<br><span class="placeholder">[Landlord mailing address]</span></p>
<p><strong>Re: Return of security deposit for 12 Elm St, Unit 4B</strong></p>
<p>Dear Pat Owner,</p>
<p>I rented 12 Elm St, Unit 4B and moved in on 2026-01-02. I moved out on 2027-01-01. I am writing to ask that my security deposit of $2,000.00 be returned in full, or that you send an itemized list of any deductions.</p>
<p>In California, landlords generally have 21 days after move-out to return the deposit. Itemized statement and any refund are both due within 21 days. By that rule the deposit is due around 2027-01-22. Source: https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=CIV&amp;sectionNum=1950.5.</p>
<p>I documented the unit's condition at move-in and at move-out. 2 items were recorded in the same or better condition at move-out.</p>
<p>The comparison marks 2 items as being in worse condition at move-out than at move-in. I list them here so we can discuss them openly, and I ask that any deduction for them be itemized with receipts or estimates and reflect only damage beyond normal wear and tear:</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Room</th><th>Item</th><th>Move-in</th><th>Move-out</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Kitchen</td><td>Oven</td><td>Good</td><td>Damaged</td><td>Scorch mark on door</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bath</td><td>Mirror</td><td>Good</td><td>Fair</td><td></td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>The deductions claimed against the deposit total $200.01:</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Deduction</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Oven</td><td>$150.00</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mirror</td><td>$50.01</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>After any deductions, we expect a total refund of $1,799.99, split between the people on the lease as follows:</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Person</th><th>Expected refund</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Sam Renter</td><td>$974.99</td></tr>
<tr><td>Alex Mate</td><td>$825.00</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>The attached move-in vs move-out comparison report has dated photos of the unit with server timestamps. It can be checked with verification code abcdef012345 at unscratched.app/v/abcdef012345.</p>
<p>Please send the deposit to <span class="placeholder">[Forwarding address]</span>. Thank you for your help.</p>
<p>Sincerely,<br>Sam Renter</p>
</body>
</html>
"
`;
